te C can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education, creates positive atmosphere, understands complicated technology. Candidate D responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but weak leadership, hot temper.\n\nWe need to make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing prior discussion (Agent 1's recommendation for B). We could raise concerns about B's cooperation and communication, and compare with other candidates. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate C creates positive atmosphere and good decision making, but has communication difficulty. Or Candidate D has responsibility and concentration, but hot temper.\n\nWe could ask a tool for missing info: e.g., ask Agent 1 about B's crew cooperation and communication. But we have note that B can be uncooperative and makes nasty remarks. That's already in our notes. So we can bring that up.\n\nWe could also ask Agent 2 for stress resilience of Candidate C or D. But we have some notes: D responds to unexpected events adequately (maybe stress). C's stress resilience unknown.\n\nWe need to keep it concise. Perhaps we argue that while B has strong reliability and technical, the cooperation concerns are serious for cockpit environment, and Candidate C, despite communication difficulty, creates positive atmosphere and makes quick correct decisions, which may outweigh B's issues. Or Candidate D has strong responsibility and concentration, but hot temper.\n\nWe need to give our vote. Could we change vote? Possibly we could still vote B but note concerns. Or we could shift to C or D. Let's evaluate: B: strong reliability, stress, technical, but uncooperative, nasty remarks, pretentious, weak memory for numbers. Those are serious for crew cooperation and attention. C: quick correct decisions, positive atmosphere, understands tech, but difficulty communicating, egocentric, not