silience), can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, weak leadership, hot temper. Also we have no direct crew cooperation observation, but weak leadership and hot temper could affect.\n\nWe need to compare D with B and C perhaps. We have concerns about B's cooperation (uncooperative, nasty remarks). D's cooperation unknown but potential issues. Also D's hot temper is a concern. B's strengths: reliability, stress, technical, decision quality. D's strengths: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, stress handling adequate. Weaknesses: hot temper, weak leadership, unknown crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to decide vote. Likely still B, but we could consider D if we think D's strengths outweigh B's cooperation issues. However D's hot temper is serious. B's uncooperative behavior is also serious. Which is worse? Both are concerns. B also has weak memory for numbers, pretentiousness. D's hot temper may affect crew. D's responsibility is strong. But B's reliability and stress handling are stronger.\n\nThus I will keep vote for B, but note we need more info on D's crew cooperation. I will argue that while D shows good responsibility and problem solving, the hot temper and weak leadership raise concerns that may be as serious as B's documented uncooperative behavior. Therefore I still recommend B, but we should probe D further.\n\nThus public message: agree with bringing D, summarize D's strengths and concerns, compare with B, state my vote B.\n\nProceed."}
